% ==================== 4. POSSIBLE CAUSES OF DAMAGE ====================
\section{Possible Causes of Damage}
 
The panel doors were inspected at the warehouse before loading, and no damage was observed on the panel doors at that time. No photographic record was taken during that inspection because photos are only taken when damage is identified.
 
Upon arrival at the site, the right and left panel doors were found dented. The chiller was transported on a trailer and secured with chains attached to the unit. The panel doors were not protected with any wrapping, foam, or bracing during transportation. The chains were most likely tightened too tightly against the chiller body, causing the dent on the panel doors.
 
The team was present at the site when the chiller was lifted from the trailer to the chiller landing platform and observed no problem during that stage. Therefore, the damage most probably occurred during the loading of the chiller onto the trailer, when the chains were secured.
 
In summary, the possible causes of the damage are:
\begin{itemize}
    \item The chiller was secured using chains on the trailer without any protective wrapping or bracing on the panel doors.
    \item The chains were tightened too tightly against the chiller body.
    \item The damage most probably occurred during loading onto the trailer, as no issue was observed during unloading and lifting at the site.
\end{itemize}
 
