% ==================== 5. REPAIRABILITY ASSESSMENT ====================
\section{Repairability Assessment}
 
The dented panel doors are repairable. The damage is limited to the outer skin of the panel door and the frame that holds the door. The door can still be closed, but it is difficult to open due to the misalignment caused by the dent and the bent frame.
 
The intended repair method is panel beating or dent pulling to restore the shape of the dented area, followed by adjustment of the door so that it opens smoothly. The plan is to tap the dented part back into shape, and not to replace the panel door.
 
The following repair approach is proposed:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Panel beating or dent pulling on the dented area of the right and left panel doors.
    \item Adjustment of the door frame and hinge alignment so that the door opens smoothly.
    \item Verification that the door closes and latches correctly after repair.
\end{itemize}
 
No replacement of the panel doors is required.
 
