% ==================== 9. CONCLUSION ====================
\section{Conclusion}
 
This report documents the damage found on the panel doors of Chiller 3 upon arrival at the SGW Google Data Center site. Both the right and left panel doors are dented, and the frame that holds the door is bent. The door can be closed, but it is difficult to open, which obstructs inspection and maintenance work.
 
The damage is repairable by panel beating or dent pulling, followed by adjustment of the door so that it opens smoothly. No replacement of the panel doors is required. The dent does not affect the airflow or cooling performance of the chiller.
 
The Samsung inspection team confirmed that there are no other damages besides the dented panel doors and minor rusted parts, which can be treated by spraying. Preventive measures, including improved packing and protection during transportation and enhanced inspection protocols, are recommended to avoid similar damage in the future.
 
